  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Goalkeeper – bonus penalty after every goal",
  "description": "Five against five, four outfield players and a goalkeeper in each team, on a pitch about 30 metres long and 25 metres wide. The goals are cone goals, about five metres wide. A goal only counts if the ball goes in along the ground or below the height of the cones – so every shot is a low one.\n\nEvery time a team scores in open play it also gets a penalty against the same goal, from about seven metres. The players take turns to take it. The same rule applies: only low balls count. The penalty is not a break in play – if the keeper saves, play carries straight on, and rebounds count.\n\nPlay periods of five minutes and count both goals from play and penalty goals. Variation: teams also get a bonus penalty instead of a corner. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stand still and big while the taker runs up – don’t go too early."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Low ball: step diagonally forward towards the ball and go down hands first."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Back on your feet straight after the save – the rebound is live."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you give a rebound, push it out wide, not back into the middle."
    }
  ],
